            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Arabic for to host, then the Arabic for a spokesperson."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: أسطورة",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أسطورة — usṭūra — \"a legend\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سمعنا أسطورة عن جبل قديم. samiʿnā usṭūra ʿan jabal qadīm. We heard a legend about an old mountain."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: أساطير, asāṭīr."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أسطورة (usṭūra) is filed by Lane under the root s-ṭ-r, \"a line of writing\", and its plural asāṭīr is old. It was borrowed from Greek historia, \"an inquiry, a story\" (EtymDB); others see a native word, so the origin is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
