          "title": "You'll want to know: بطل",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بطل — baṭal — \"a hero; a champion\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "كان جدي بطلا في قريته. kāna jaddī baṭalan fī qaryatihi. My grandfather was a hero in his village."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: أبطال, abṭāl."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In sport بطل (baṭal) is a champion, and the hero of a film or novel is its بطل (baṭal) too."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بطل (baṭal) is built on the native Arabic root b-ṭ-l (Lane), \"to come to nothing\". Lane explains baṭal, a brave man, as one whose wound goes for nothing, so that it does not hold him back."
            }
          ]
        },
